      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that $\\tan x = 2$, we are asked to find $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)$. Using the tangent addition formula, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\n\nSince we know $\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1$, we substitute $\\tan x = 2$ into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{-3}$.",
