    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that \\(\\tan x = 2\\), we want to find \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\).\n\nWe use the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan (A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\nHere, \\(A = x\\) and \\(B = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\). We know that \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\). Therefore, we can substitute \\(\\tan x = 2\\) and \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\) into the formula:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}} = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) is \\(\\boxed{-3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this by implementing it in Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given tan(x) = 2\ntan_x = 2\n\n# Using the tangent addition formula\ntan_π_over_4 = 1\nresult = (tan_x + tan_π_over_4) / (1 - tan_x * tan_π_over_4)\nprint(result)\n```",
